(null, null, 'Thomas Aquinas attempted to synthesize Aristotelian philosophy with Christian theology, arguing that reason and faith are ultimately compatible paths toward truth.', 'Thomas Aquinas', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'The ''social contract'' theory proposes that legitimate political authority derives from an implicit agreement among individuals to form a society and government for mutual benefit.', 'Hobbes', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'Ayn Rand''s philosophy of Objectivism argues that rational self-interest, rather than altruism, should be the guiding moral principle for human behavior.', 'Ayn Rand', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'The ''problem of induction'' questions whether we''re logically justified in assuming the future will resemble the past, since no amount of past observation can guarantee future outcomes.', 'David Hume', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'Jean-Jacques Rousseau argued that humans are naturally good but corrupted by the artificial structures and inequalities introduced by society.', 'Jean-Jacques Rousseau', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'The ''Gettier problem'' challenges the classical definition of knowledge as ''justified true belief'' by presenting scenarios where someone has a justified true belief that still seems to fail as genuine knowledge.', 'Edmund Gettier', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'Pragmatism, an American philosophical tradition, holds that the truth or meaning of an idea is tied to its practical consequences and usefulness in action.', 'William James', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'The ''ethical egoism'' position holds that individuals morally ought to act in their own self-interest, distinct from the merely descriptive claim that people generally do act selfishly.', 'Ethical egoism scholarship', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'Simone de Beauvoir and Jean-Paul Sartre''s existentialist philosophy emphasized radical freedom, arguing humans are ''condemned to be free'' and fully responsible for their own choices.', 'Sartre and de Beauvoir', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'The ''paradox of the stone'' asks whether an omnipotent being could create a stone so heavy that even it could not lift it, probing the logical limits of the concept of omnipotence.', 'Philosophy of religion', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'Epictetus, a Stoic philosopher born into slavery, taught that true freedom comes from controlling one''s own judgments rather than external circumstances beyond one''s control.', 'Epictetus', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'The ''is-ought problem'' remains central to debates over whether moral facts can be objectively grounded in the natural world or are fundamentally different in kind from factual claims.', 'David Hume and metaethical scholarship', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'Niccolò Machiavelli''s The Prince controversially argued that political leaders should sometimes prioritize effective, even ruthless, action over conventional moral virtue to maintain stable rule.', 'Niccolò Machiavelli', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'The ''Experience Machine'' thought experiment asks whether you would plug into a machine simulating a perfect, pleasurable life, questioning whether we value authentic experience over mere pleasure.', 'Robert Nozick', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'Zen Buddhism emphasizes direct, intuitive insight over scriptural study alone, often using paradoxical riddles called koans to push students beyond ordinary logical thinking.', 'Zen Buddhist philosophical tradition', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'The ''paradox of free will and divine foreknowledge'' asks how humans can have genuine free will if an all-knowing God already knows every choice they will ever make.', 'Philosophy of religion', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'Edmund Husserl''s phenomenology sought to describe conscious experience precisely as it is lived, bracketing out assumptions about an external objective reality.', 'Edmund Husserl', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'The ''repugnant conclusion'' in population ethics suggests that, under certain utilitarian assumptions, a world with an enormous population living barely worthwhile lives could be considered better than a smaller, flourishing population.', 'Derek Parfit', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'Lao Tzu''s Taoist philosophy emphasizes simplicity, humility, and living in harmony with the natural order rather than imposing rigid structures or excessive ambition.', 'Laozi', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'The ''paradox of fiction'' asks why we feel genuine emotional responses, like sadness or fear, toward characters and events we know are not real.', 'Aesthetic philosophy', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'Peter Singer''s utilitarian ethics extends moral consideration to animals, arguing that the capacity to suffer, not species membership alone, should determine moral status.', 'Peter Singer', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'The ''paradox of omniscience,'' related to debates about foreknowledge, questions whether a being who knows the future with certainty can meaningfully be said to make free choices.', 'Philosophy of religion scholarship', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'Hannah Arendt''s concept of the ''banality of evil'' suggested that great atrocities can be committed not by monstrous villains but by ordinary people simply following orders without critical reflection.', 'Hannah Arendt', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'The ''no self'' doctrine in Buddhist philosophy holds that what we call the ''self'' is actually a constantly shifting bundle of physical and mental processes, with no fixed, permanent essence.', 'Buddhist philosophy', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'John Stuart Mill argued that individual liberty should be protected except when one''s actions cause direct harm to others, a principle known as the harm principle.', 'John Stuart Mill', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'The ''paradox of self-reference'' appears throughout logic and philosophy, as seen in statements or systems that refer to or evaluate themselves, sometimes producing unresolvable contradictions.', 'Mathematical logic and philosophy scholarship', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'Georg Cantor''s philosophical and mathematical work on different sizes of infinity challenged long-held assumptions, showing that some infinities are provably larger than others.', 'Georg Cantor', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'The ''veil of maya'' in Hindu philosophy describes the illusion that obscures the true, unified nature of reality behind the apparent multiplicity of the everyday world.', 'Hindu Vedantic philosophy', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'Bertrand Russell''s paradox exposed a deep contradiction in naive set theory by asking whether the ''set of all sets that do not contain themselves'' contains itself.', 'Bertrand Russell', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'The ''Ship of Theseus'' thought experiment extends into questions of digital identity, asking whether a mind gradually uploaded or replaced piece by piece with digital components remains the same person.', 'Modern philosophy of mind', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'Confucian philosophy''s concept of ''ren,'' often translated as benevolence or humaneness, is considered the central virtue underlying all other ethical behavior in Confucian thought.', 'Confucius', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'The ''paradox of value,'' also called the diamond-water paradox, asks why water, essential for life, is cheap, while diamonds, largely non-essential, are expensive.', 'Adam Smith', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'Simone Weil argued that affliction, severe and prolonged suffering, can either destroy a person''s soul or, paradoxically, open a profound path toward spiritual understanding.', 'Simone Weil', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'The ''problem of personal identity over time'' asks what, if anything, makes the person you are today truly identical to the person you were as a young child, given how much has changed.', 'Derek Parfit', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'Friedrich Nietzsche''s concept of ''eternal recurrence'' asks you to imagine living your exact life over and over infinitely, as a thought experiment for evaluating whether you genuinely affirm your life.', 'Friedrich Nietzsche', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'The ''is-ought problem'' has prompted some philosophers to argue for ''moral naturalism,'' the view that ethical facts can, in fact, be reduced to or derived from natural, scientific facts.', 'Metaethical naturalism scholarship', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'Baruch Spinoza''s deterministic philosophy argued that true freedom comes not from an illusory free will, but from rationally understanding the necessary causes behind our emotions and actions.', 'Baruch Spinoza', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'The ''trolley problem'' has been adapted into dozens of variations by philosophers, including scenarios involving pushing a person directly versus pulling a lever, to probe subtle moral intuitions about causation and intention.', 'Philippa Foot and Judith Jarvis Thomson', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now()),
(null, null, 'Simone de Beauvoir''s existentialist ethics argued that genuine freedom requires actively willing the freedom of others, not just pursuing one''s own.', 'Simone de Beauvoir', 'philosophy', array['philosophy'], 'approved', 'import:csv', now());
